00:43:57.552 --> 00:43:59.804
WITH TILE 6, THE SUM WILL REACH 21

00:43:59.887 --> 00:44:01.889
Are there more Tile 6s
other than the one above Tile 11?

00:44:01.973 --> 00:44:04.016
There's one more in the upper left corner.

00:44:04.100 --> 00:44:07.812
You're right.
It looks like Jong-yun can wrap it up now.

00:44:08.020 --> 00:44:11.566
Team KAIST's Jeon Ji-min.
Please move the piece.

00:44:18.614 --> 00:44:20.950
You have ten seconds left.

00:44:26.998 --> 00:44:28.457
I'll obtain the tile.

00:44:30.710 --> 00:44:32.962
JEON JI-MIN:
9, 1, 4, 5,

00:44:34.422 --> 00:44:38.176
I managed to get to the 3-3 tie
and claimed Tile 4 as I planned.

00:44:38.259 --> 00:44:40.928
All I needed to win then was Tile 16.

00:44:41.679 --> 00:44:45.850
JONG-YUN DISCARDED TILE 16

00:44:48.019 --> 00:44:51.939
I thought, "That will get me the victory.
I'm on the brink of winning."

00:44:53.441 --> 00:44:56.194
Team SNU in STEM's Han Jong-yun.
Please move the piece.

00:44:58.779 --> 00:44:59.989
I'll obtain the tile.

00:45:01.365 --> 00:45:03.075
HAN JONG-YUN:
9, 4, CLOVER 6

00:45:03.159 --> 00:45:05.661
Team KAIST's Jeon Ji-min.
Please move the piece.

00:45:08.331 --> 00:45:09.832
Please make your choice.

00:45:10.124 --> 00:45:11.292
I'll discard my Tile 5.

00:45:15.171 --> 00:45:17.256
Come on now. Surely not...

00:45:21.302 --> 00:45:23.262
BOTH TEAMS NEED JUST ONE MORE TILE TO WIN

00:45:23.346 --> 00:45:25.723
JONG-YUN'S TARGET: TILE 6
JI-MIN'S TARGET: TILE 16

00:45:30.186 --> 00:45:31.729
Please make your choice.

00:45:31.812 --> 00:45:33.231
I'll discard my Tile 4.

00:45:40.488 --> 00:45:42.615
Jong-yun can reach that Tile 6
no matter what.

00:45:42.698 --> 00:45:45.868
Ji-min can't reverse Jong-yun's last move,
so he won't have any problem.

00:45:45.952 --> 00:45:48.287
As the piece cannot be returned

00:45:48.371 --> 00:45:50.164
to its original place
from the previous turn,

00:45:50.248 --> 00:45:54.210
Team KAIST's Jeon Ji-min can only take it
within the highlighted area.

00:45:54.752 --> 00:45:56.837
Regardless of where he leaves it,

00:45:56.921 --> 00:46:01.801
Team SNU in STEM's Han Jong-yun
can obtain Tile 6 on his next turn.

00:46:06.639 --> 00:46:07.807
Please make your choice.

00:46:07.890 --> 00:46:09.934
I'll take a pass.

00:46:10.017 --> 00:46:13.271
Team SNU in STEM's Han Jong-yun.
Please move the piece.

00:46:15.940 --> 00:46:17.024
Please make your choice.

00:46:17.108 --> 00:46:18.234
I'll obtain the tile.

00:46:25.116 --> 00:46:28.786
Team SNU in STEM's Han Jong-yun
logged a set of tiles.

00:46:28.869 --> 00:46:30.997
He won a point.

00:46:43.509 --> 00:46:45.469
I'm floored.

00:46:46.721 --> 00:46:50.808
I was glad that I managed to repay
my teammates' trust with a victory.

00:46:50.891 --> 00:46:51.976
I also felt relieved.

00:46:52.059 --> 00:46:55.146
I was literally one tile away
from winning,

00:46:55.229 --> 00:46:56.731
so I was racing to get it.

00:46:56.814 --> 00:47:00.151
It was deeply upsetting
to have it slip through my fingers.

00:47:04.613 --> 00:47:08.075
Team SNU in STEM's Han Jong-yun
won four points in total.

00:47:08.159 --> 00:47:10.536
That concludes Round 3 of Lucky 21.

00:47:10.619 --> 00:47:13.748
Round 3 ends
with Team SNU in STEM's victory.

00:47:14.582 --> 00:47:16.667
- Thanks for the good game.
- Thank you.

00:47:22.506 --> 00:47:24.050
- Good job.
- Thanks, man.

00:47:27.636 --> 00:47:29.930
All I needed was one more turn.

00:47:30.014 --> 00:47:32.183
- What a shame.
- It's so disappointing.

00:47:32.266 --> 00:47:34.894
- Thank you for your trust.
- I loved your game.

00:47:34.977 --> 00:47:37.855
You were amazing.

00:47:37.938 --> 00:47:42.151
That concludes the Deathmatch, Lucky 21.

00:47:45.154 --> 00:47:48.366
The third team to be eliminated
from Elite League Season 3 is

00:47:48.741 --> 00:47:50.618
Team KAIST.

00:47:50.993 --> 00:47:52.953
Will the light go out?

00:47:53.037 --> 00:47:56.040
Oh, no. Don't turn off
the lovely sky blue light.

00:47:56.749 --> 00:47:58.584
All teams surrounding us went home.

00:47:59.085 --> 00:48:00.503
So lonely.

00:48:00.586 --> 00:48:03.047
- I haven't had a face-off against Ji-hu.
- Oh, right.

00:48:06.342 --> 00:48:09.720
Team KAIST, please exit the grounds.

00:48:10.638 --> 00:48:12.431
- Should we get going?
- Yeah.

00:48:12.515 --> 00:48:15.935
- Are we seriously leaving?
- Bummer.

00:48:24.693 --> 00:48:25.903
It's such a shame.

00:48:27.363 --> 00:48:28.197
Let's do our best.

00:48:28.280 --> 00:48:30.408
Our clips will be on the web
for at least a decade.

00:48:31.158 --> 00:48:32.201
This should be fun.

00:48:32.284 --> 00:48:35.704
I basically waited two years
to be on the show, since I applied twice.

00:48:35.788 --> 00:48:39.250
Team KAIST's Jeon Ji-min
has been chosen as the Ace player.

00:48:40.126 --> 00:48:41.669
I was so elated to be selected.

00:48:41.752 --> 00:48:44.713
I had such a great time
playing the amazing games.

00:48:45.047 --> 00:48:47.049
The two-year wait was so worth it.

00:48:49.593 --> 00:48:50.678
...was correct.

00:48:52.388 --> 00:48:55.141
My only regret is
that our joyful journey has to end.

00:48:55.683 --> 00:48:57.059
What a bummer.

00:48:57.435 --> 00:49:01.856
Thanks to my teammates, I made it so far
and got to play a bunch of fun games.

00:49:01.939 --> 00:49:04.316
Now, we have to leave...

00:49:05.192 --> 00:49:06.986
I still can't believe it.

00:49:07.570 --> 00:49:11.323
I gave it my all until the end,
so I don't have any regrets left.

00:49:11.407 --> 00:49:13.993
I'd like to thank the creators
for the opportunity.

00:49:15.119 --> 00:49:18.122
Jae-han is a wiz with this stuff.
He's like a machine.

00:49:18.456 --> 00:49:21.167
I probably wasn't the strongest contender,

00:49:21.250 --> 00:49:24.295
but I loved tackling various tasks
with the help of my team.

00:49:24.378 --> 00:49:28.132
I had so much fun competing here
with my teammates by my side.

00:49:28.215 --> 00:49:30.509
I think I'll remember
my days here forever.

00:49:30.593 --> 00:49:35.931
To be honest,
being on the show felt like a dream.

00:49:36.015 --> 00:49:37.433
Along the way...

00:49:37.516 --> 00:49:41.312
This is probably the day I solved
the most calculation questions in my life.

00:49:41.395 --> 00:49:43.898
I do have my regrets,
but I did my very best.

00:49:43.981 --> 00:49:47.359
My teammates also gave their all,
so I want to thank them for it.

00:49:51.906 --> 00:49:53.491
I'm sorry.

00:49:53.574 --> 00:49:54.533
- Don't be.
- My bad.

00:49:54.617 --> 00:49:56.827
Don't say that.
You're here because you are good.

00:49:57.161 --> 00:49:58.287
Excuse me.

00:49:58.370 --> 00:49:59.788
We're splitting the prize, remember?

00:50:14.220 --> 00:50:16.597
We'll have the 1-on-1 interviews now.

00:50:16.680 --> 00:50:17.723
AFTER LUCKY 21

00:50:17.932 --> 00:50:20.267
If you wait at the main hall...

00:50:20.351 --> 00:50:24.063
ALL CONTESTANTS GATHER AT THE MAIN HALL

00:50:24.313 --> 00:50:26.607
TEAM KAIST
THIRD TEAM TO BE ELIMINATED

00:50:26.690 --> 00:50:27.650
They turned the lights off.

00:50:27.733 --> 00:50:29.777
LIGHTS ARE OFF
OUTSIDE THE ELIMINATED TEAMS' BASE CAMPS

00:50:29.860 --> 00:50:32.071
WAILING

00:50:32.321 --> 00:50:34.323
Hey, the lights are off.

00:50:34.782 --> 00:50:36.158
- They turned off the light.
- I know.

00:50:36.242 --> 00:50:37.701
TEAM POSTECH
FIRST TEAM TO BE ELIMINATED

00:50:37.993 --> 00:50:39.411
I hear you came in first.

00:50:39.495 --> 00:50:41.455
TEAM YONSEI
SECOND TEAM TO BE ELIMINATED

00:50:42.039 --> 00:50:43.457
So you killed it?

00:50:43.791 --> 00:50:45.084
- It's been a while.
- Right.

00:50:45.167 --> 00:50:47.253
- So you aced the main match?
- Yes, we did.

00:50:47.336 --> 00:50:49.171
Tae-hun did the heavy lifting.

00:50:49.255 --> 00:50:50.256
Be the champions, okay?

00:50:50.339 --> 00:50:52.925
It's 2-against-1 now. You've got to win.

00:50:53.008 --> 00:50:54.343
You bet we will.

00:50:54.426 --> 00:50:56.178
We can't let Team SNU
win three seasons in a row.

00:50:56.262 --> 00:50:57.471
Exactly.

00:50:58.722 --> 00:51:00.140
You guys are my favorite.

00:51:00.683 --> 00:51:02.560
- You're my favorite, okay?
- The feeling's mutual.

00:51:03.143 --> 00:51:05.604
We had good chemistry, didn't we?

00:51:06.021 --> 00:51:08.274
I'm sorry.
If we hadn't bungled the main match...

00:51:08.357 --> 00:51:11.193
We should've done a better job
with the investigation.

00:51:12.319 --> 00:51:14.738
How was the shoot yesterday?
Aren't you guys drained?

00:51:14.822 --> 00:51:16.740
I went straight to bed after Day 1.

00:51:16.824 --> 00:51:18.576
And I woke up at 3 p.m. the day after.

00:51:19.118 --> 00:51:20.286
- I was that tired.
- Sounds lovely.

00:51:20.369 --> 00:51:21.537
I'm so jealous.

00:51:21.787 --> 00:51:24.290
You think it was lovely?
Are you making fun of us?

00:51:25.624 --> 00:51:27.376
We are just messing with you.

00:51:27.459 --> 00:51:29.420
What did you do at the hotel?

00:51:29.753 --> 00:51:30.629
Us?

00:51:30.713 --> 00:51:32.715
We wallowed in grief.

00:51:33.090 --> 00:51:34.341
We grieved.

00:51:34.425 --> 00:51:36.677
To be honest, I fell asleep right away,

00:51:36.760 --> 00:51:38.971
but these folks had a sleepless night.

00:51:39.054 --> 00:51:41.557
I finally fell asleep at 5 a.m.

00:51:41.640 --> 00:51:44.268
A-in's crying face kept coming back to me.

00:51:45.853 --> 00:51:47.563
Of course, you were heartbroken.

00:51:47.896 --> 00:51:50.441
- It was upsetting.
- We were heartsick.

00:51:50.524 --> 00:51:51.567
So, Ji-hu.

00:51:51.650 --> 00:51:53.694
- You went to Hansung Science High?
- Yes.

00:51:53.777 --> 00:51:55.821
- You graduated early, too?
- Yes.

00:51:55.904 --> 00:51:56.739
KANG JI-HU, 17 YEARS OLD

00:51:56.822 --> 00:51:59.366
How are you so bright when you're only 17?

00:52:00.159 --> 00:52:02.161
His brain is young and supple.

00:52:02.244 --> 00:52:04.955
- Back when I was 18...
- We were beasts.

00:52:05.372 --> 00:52:06.457
We shook the whole universe.

00:52:06.540 --> 00:52:09.585
- We will now begin a redemption round.
- What?

00:52:12.463 --> 00:52:13.631
- Wait...
- Seriously?

00:52:15.132 --> 00:52:16.925
What on earth?

00:52:18.510 --> 00:52:19.678
Is this for real?

00:52:19.762 --> 00:52:21.263
It makes no sense.

00:52:21.347 --> 00:52:22.681
Is this for real?

00:52:22.765 --> 00:52:24.350
Seriously, what's going on?

00:52:26.935 --> 00:52:28.812
- It's real.
- Are you serious?

00:52:28.896 --> 00:52:31.273
What was our elimination interview for?

00:52:36.153 --> 00:52:37.571
What on earth?

00:52:37.655 --> 00:52:38.989
Maybe the game is on today.

00:52:39.073 --> 00:52:41.116
- It's on right away.
- Right away?

00:52:41.200 --> 00:52:42.701
The whole interview was a smoke screen.

00:52:42.785 --> 00:52:45.371
They used it as a pretext
for the redemption round.

00:52:46.955 --> 00:52:48.374
- Hang on.
- Just a second.

00:52:48.457 --> 00:52:50.334
- Let's put our friendship on hold.
- Yeah, right.

00:52:50.417 --> 00:52:52.294
We'll see you later.

00:52:52.586 --> 00:52:54.463
We have a good chance of making it back.

00:52:54.546 --> 00:52:56.006
We've got to take it.

00:52:56.090 --> 00:52:58.717
Seriously though, we need you to advance.

00:52:58.801 --> 00:53:01.178
- That way, we get a 3-to-1 setup.
- "Medical versus STEM,

00:53:01.261 --> 00:53:03.597
- med students flatten their opponents."
- We need that.

00:53:04.598 --> 00:53:06.934
Let's give it our all
like it's our Deathmatch.

00:53:07.017 --> 00:53:09.228
A true Deathmatch
where the survivors return from hell.

00:53:10.521 --> 00:53:12.398
This is exactly what we needed.

00:53:12.731 --> 00:53:16.402
We will now begin the redemption round.

00:53:16.985 --> 00:53:18.862
Oh, the lights are back on.

00:53:21.240 --> 00:53:22.449
They turned them back on.

00:53:22.533 --> 00:53:24.410
- Wow, the lights are on.
- They are.

00:53:25.077 --> 00:53:26.328
Team POSTECH.

00:53:26.912 --> 00:53:27.996
Team Yonsei.

00:53:28.580 --> 00:53:29.748
Team KAIST.

00:53:30.290 --> 00:53:32.710
With the exception of these three teams,

00:53:32.793 --> 00:53:35.629
please return to your base camps.

00:53:35.713 --> 00:53:36.547
Good luck, Team Yonsei!

00:53:36.630 --> 00:53:38.590
- You've got this!
- Go get them!

00:53:38.674 --> 00:53:40.384
- Good luck!
- You've got this!

00:53:40.467 --> 00:53:41.510
All right!

00:53:42.136 --> 00:53:43.595
- Good luck.
- Go get them!

00:53:43.679 --> 00:53:45.055
Let's go, STEM Division!

00:53:45.139 --> 00:53:46.181
We'll do our best!

00:53:46.515 --> 00:53:47.349
Ji-hoo.

00:53:47.433 --> 00:53:48.684
Hey, Ji-hoo.

00:53:48.767 --> 00:53:50.519
FROM JI-HU TO JI-HOO
Good luck.

00:53:50.602 --> 00:53:51.437
You've got this.

00:53:51.520 --> 00:53:52.896
All right. Go, me!

00:53:54.106 --> 00:53:56.191
This isn't exactly good news for us.

00:53:56.275 --> 00:53:57.901
- I agree.
- Same here.

00:53:57.985 --> 00:54:00.070
Things will get tricky
with Team KAIST back in the mix.

00:54:00.154 --> 00:54:02.531
We barely managed to defeat them.

00:54:02.614 --> 00:54:04.032
They're way too good.

00:54:04.116 --> 00:54:06.785
We jumped through hoops
to get them eliminated.

00:54:07.536 --> 00:54:09.079
If Team Yonsei makes it back,

00:54:09.163 --> 00:54:11.123
- it will get rough for us.
- I know.

00:54:11.206 --> 00:54:13.751
- We had such a close game.
- Exactly.

00:54:13.834 --> 00:54:15.753
We won by a very narrow margin.

00:54:15.836 --> 00:54:18.255
Who knows what will happen in a rematch?

00:54:18.338 --> 00:54:21.592
Honestly though,
I was happy to see Team Yonsei leave.

00:54:21.675 --> 00:54:25.220
This means
that we get one of our rivals back.

00:54:25.304 --> 00:54:26.138
Tell me about it.

00:54:26.638 --> 00:54:27.931
That will add the pressure.

00:54:28.307 --> 00:54:30.934
None of them is a pushover.
It's frightening.

00:54:31.018 --> 00:54:32.644
A true return from hell.

00:54:32.728 --> 00:54:33.812
A redemption round?

00:54:33.896 --> 00:54:36.982
But then again, it did feel like
things were going too well.

00:54:37.733 --> 00:54:39.151
I wonder which team will make it back.

00:54:39.234 --> 00:54:42.946
I think Team KAIST has the upper hand
since they played until this morning.

00:54:43.030 --> 00:54:44.698
They could be worn out, though.

00:54:44.782 --> 00:54:47.034
Team Yonsei had a good night's rest.

00:54:47.117 --> 00:54:50.746
Let's say Team KAIST manages to advance.
Just imagine their day.

00:54:50.829 --> 00:54:53.582
They would've traveled back and forth
from hell to heaven.

00:54:54.082 --> 00:54:56.752
I still can't believe what's happening.

00:54:56.835 --> 00:55:00.756
Our elimination was a surprise,
but that was nothing compared to this.

00:55:01.215 --> 00:55:03.383
Those guys look so well-rested.

00:55:06.762 --> 00:55:08.347
We're at a disadvantage.

00:55:08.430 --> 00:55:10.557
That's true.
But we must rise above and win

00:55:10.641 --> 00:55:12.518
to complete our hero's journey.

00:55:12.601 --> 00:55:14.269
We'll overcome this.

00:55:15.103 --> 00:55:18.565
We simply couldn't get eliminated again.
I was determined to claw our way back.

00:55:18.649 --> 00:55:21.693
Let's pull ourselves together
and do better this time.

00:55:21.777 --> 00:55:24.404
Let's give it our all
and leave no regrets.

00:55:24.863 --> 00:55:28.617
That was our last shot.
Another defeat meant we were truly done.

00:55:28.909 --> 00:55:31.787
We'll win this time
and make our way back into the game.

00:55:32.746 --> 00:55:34.164
Remember how it felt when we got axed.

00:55:34.248 --> 00:55:35.791
- Let's do our best.
- I'm all for that.

00:55:35.874 --> 00:55:37.000
Imagine how cool it'd be

00:55:37.084 --> 00:55:39.336
if we rose like a phoenix
and became the champions.

00:55:39.419 --> 00:55:40.254
Totally.

00:55:40.337 --> 00:55:42.506
- That's a perfect narrative.
- You bet.

00:55:42.965 --> 00:55:46.385
I wanted to win no matter what.
I was ready to seize my shot.

00:55:46.844 --> 00:55:48.428
The redemption round is...

00:55:54.268 --> 00:55:56.019
Relay Match.

00:55:58.146 --> 00:55:59.815
It's called the Relay Match.

00:56:00.107 --> 00:56:01.400
It will be a one-on-one game.

00:56:01.483 --> 00:56:03.777
Everyone will have to pull their weight.

00:56:04.111 --> 00:56:05.362
In Relay Match,

00:56:05.445 --> 00:56:09.408
the host will choose 1 game
out of 3 options.

00:56:09.491 --> 00:56:12.995
Then, they will select one contestant
as their opponent.

00:56:13.078 --> 00:56:15.914
The winner will be determined
by the head-to-head results.

00:56:22.254 --> 00:56:25.799
An individual competition is long overdue.
The survivors should be the fittest.

00:56:26.174 --> 00:56:29.428
Given the setup, one person
may single-handedly rescue their team.

00:56:29.511 --> 00:56:30.762
This will be so much fun.

00:56:30.846 --> 00:56:34.766
All teams will be assigned six lives.

00:56:34.850 --> 00:56:38.729
You can freely divide them
between your teammates,

00:56:38.812 --> 00:56:42.608
but please remember to assign
at least one life to each member.

00:56:42.900 --> 00:56:44.276
This sounds so exciting.

00:56:44.359 --> 00:56:46.278
- Won't Ji-min get three lives?
- Maybe.

00:56:46.361 --> 00:56:48.363
They'll need to approach it strategically.

00:56:49.031 --> 00:56:52.784
As Team KAIST
managed to survive the longest,

00:56:52.868 --> 00:56:55.120
one of their members
will be the initial host.

00:56:55.203 --> 00:56:58.165
The host can choose
the game they would like to play

00:56:58.248 --> 00:57:00.709
and the contestant
they would like to compete against.

00:57:00.918 --> 00:57:05.505
The winner's team
will be awarded one point.

00:57:05.589 --> 00:57:08.717
Additionally,
the winner will be the next host.

00:57:09.718 --> 00:57:13.055
The loser will lose one life.

00:57:13.138 --> 00:57:15.682
When you lose all your lives,

00:57:15.766 --> 00:57:18.810
you will be barred
from participating in the game.

00:57:20.270 --> 00:57:21.647
It's a true fight to the death.

00:57:21.730 --> 00:57:23.857
We'll get an all-out war.

00:57:23.941 --> 00:57:25.651
The games will test you

00:57:25.734 --> 00:57:29.237
on reasoning, spatial awareness,
and memorization.

00:57:29.321 --> 00:57:34.826
Relay Match has 18 questions in total,
with 6 questions per game.

00:57:35.494 --> 00:57:41.083
Each team can use the Priority card
once throughout the entire game.

00:57:41.667 --> 00:57:44.461
Please note that it can only be used
within 30 seconds

00:57:44.544 --> 00:57:46.964
after the host's selection.

00:57:47.047 --> 00:57:51.009
The contestant who uses the Priority card
can compete against the host

00:57:51.093 --> 00:57:53.762
instead of the opponent of their choice.

00:57:55.180 --> 00:57:56.848
Like a substitute.

00:57:57.099 --> 00:57:58.976
Secure points following these rules.

00:57:59.559 --> 00:58:03.355
The team with the most points
will be declared the winner.

00:58:03.438 --> 00:58:06.233
The winning team
will get their second chance

00:58:06.316 --> 00:58:10.362
to rejoin the surviving teams
of the competition.

00:58:10.821 --> 00:58:12.197
You've got this, right?

00:58:13.281 --> 00:58:14.324
We have to do well.

00:58:15.867 --> 00:58:18.787
- Let's do this.
- We've got this.

00:58:19.246 --> 00:58:20.288
Our Ace player.

00:58:20.664 --> 00:58:22.165
We're going to win.

00:58:22.457 --> 00:58:25.502
We will now reveal the three games

00:58:25.585 --> 00:58:29.089
of the redemption round, Relay Match.

00:58:29.172 --> 00:58:32.092
The first game
will test your reasoning skills.

00:58:32.175 --> 00:58:34.011
It is Time Jump.

00:58:34.094 --> 00:58:35.345
In Time Jump,

00:58:35.429 --> 00:58:39.224
your task is to fill in each blank
with one of the given numbers.

00:58:39.307 --> 00:58:42.310
The first to make
the correct sentence wins.

00:58:42.769 --> 00:58:46.023
You may be asked about dates as well.

00:58:47.858 --> 00:58:49.609
USE NUMBERS FROM 1 TO 3
"One hour after 2 o'clock is 3 o'clock."

00:58:49.693 --> 00:58:51.153
"Two hours after 1 o'clock is 3 o'clock."

00:58:51.236 --> 00:58:52.863
There are multiple answers.

00:58:53.321 --> 00:58:56.658
The second game
will test your spatial awareness.

00:58:56.742 --> 00:58:58.326
It is Pixel Art.

00:58:58.869 --> 00:59:01.038
"Pixel"? That may be like Pixel Number.

00:59:01.121 --> 00:59:02.873
I don't get the "art" part.

00:59:02.956 --> 00:59:06.293
In Pixel Art, you will be presented
with nine pixel cards in total.

00:59:06.376 --> 00:59:09.755
Three of them will match the target
when layered together.

00:59:09.838 --> 00:59:11.965
Your task is to find them first.

00:59:12.674 --> 00:59:14.801
They have to be overlapped?

00:59:14.885 --> 00:59:16.678
Oh, that sounds like fun!

00:59:16.762 --> 00:59:18.513
When you combine the pixel cards,

00:59:18.930 --> 00:59:21.933
you can rotate the cards
to get the target image.

00:59:23.685 --> 00:59:25.645
Dang, I'm taking back what I just said.

00:59:25.729 --> 00:59:28.273
- Shoot, did I just hear right?
- Oh, man.

00:59:28.774 --> 00:59:30.317
That's tricky.

00:59:30.400 --> 00:59:36.114
But the pixel cards may not be flipped
horizontally or vertically.

00:59:36.198 --> 00:59:40.118
The three primary colors in Pixel Art
can be mixed to create secondary colors.

00:59:40.202 --> 00:59:43.163
A red cell layered over a blue cell
will result in a violet cell.

00:59:43.246 --> 00:59:46.083
A red cell layered over a yellow cell
will result in an orange cell.

00:59:46.166 --> 00:59:48.835
A blue cell layered over a yellow cell
will result in a green cell.

00:59:48.919 --> 00:59:51.713
When all three colors
are layered together,

00:59:51.797 --> 00:59:53.590
you will get a black cell.

00:59:53.673 --> 00:59:56.384
To get a secondary color,

00:59:56.468 --> 01:00:00.347
the different colors
must be mixed at a 1-to-1 ratio.

01:00:00.430 --> 01:00:04.059
But cells of the same color
can be layered without restrictions.

01:00:04.142 --> 01:00:06.103
They've got to mix the colors?

01:00:06.186 --> 01:00:08.105
That explains the art part.

01:00:08.188 --> 01:00:10.482
The black cells
will be the ones to watch out for.

01:00:10.774 --> 01:00:12.567
The black cells seem important, right?

01:00:12.651 --> 01:00:15.654
Let's use the secondary colors
as our guide.

01:00:15.737 --> 01:00:18.740
The third game
will test your memorization skills.

01:00:18.824 --> 01:00:21.535
I hope we get a decent memorization game.

01:00:21.952 --> 01:00:23.829
It is Photo Memory.

01:00:23.912 --> 01:00:25.247
In Photo Memory,

01:00:25.330 --> 01:00:28.750
you will be shown a set of 10 photos
for 10 seconds each to memorize.

01:00:30.919 --> 01:00:34.548
You will then solve
nine questions in a row.

01:00:35.132 --> 01:00:39.010
The player with more points wins the game.

01:00:40.428 --> 01:00:43.473
- What on earth? That sounds outrageous.
- That's just insane.

01:00:43.557 --> 01:00:45.433
It's not a simple memorization game.

01:00:45.517 --> 01:00:47.519
This will actually require
a photographic memory.

01:00:47.602 --> 01:00:49.271
That sounds like a blast, though.

01:00:49.604 --> 01:00:51.356
- I can crush this.
- Really?

01:00:51.439 --> 01:00:54.484
I can take down anyone
when it comes to pure brainpower shit.

01:00:54.568 --> 01:00:56.403
Watch your language.

01:00:56.570 --> 01:00:59.948
Sounds like only Pixel Art
requires strategies.

01:01:00.031 --> 01:01:02.159
As for the rest, we can rely on our minds.

01:01:02.242 --> 01:01:06.872
Here's the real problem.
What if Team KAIST won't choose us?

01:01:06.955 --> 01:01:09.166
We'll use the Priority card
and claim the host position.

01:01:09.249 --> 01:01:10.208
I see. Good idea.

01:01:11.126 --> 01:01:13.253
I guess that's what the card is for.

01:01:13.336 --> 01:01:15.714
All teams,
please start discussing your strategies.

01:01:15.797 --> 01:01:18.967
You'll be given 20 minutes.

01:01:19.926 --> 01:01:22.304
All the 1-on-1 games
were saved for this match.

01:01:22.387 --> 01:01:24.181
It looks like so much fun.

01:01:24.264 --> 01:01:27.601
This is pretty similar
to Mystery Poker from yesterday.

01:01:27.684 --> 01:01:29.227
The more prepared you are,

01:01:29.311 --> 01:01:31.188
- the less confused you get.
- Agreed.

01:01:32.731 --> 01:01:34.900
Can I tell you
about the strategy for Pixel Art first?

01:01:34.983 --> 01:01:35.817
Go ahead.

01:01:36.026 --> 01:01:38.528
We can rotate the pixel cards, right?

01:01:38.612 --> 01:01:39.946
Here's what I think.

01:01:40.030 --> 01:01:42.991
Whichever way you rotate it,
the center cell will remain in the spot.

01:01:43.074 --> 01:01:45.535
Why don't we use that as a guide
to sort out the cards?

01:01:46.286 --> 01:01:47.162
I like the idea.

01:01:47.621 --> 01:01:50.248
Look at this example.
Since the center cell is white,

01:01:50.332 --> 01:01:52.626
we can exclude the cards
with a colored cell in the center.

01:01:52.709 --> 01:01:54.961
EXCLUDE PIXEL CARDS WITH A COLORED CENTER

01:01:55.045 --> 01:01:56.087
If the center cell is black,

01:01:56.171 --> 01:01:58.506
we will need a combination
of red, yellow, and blue.

01:01:58.590 --> 01:02:01.509
RED, BLUE, AND YELLOW ARE NEEDED
TO GET THE COLOR BLACK

01:02:01.593 --> 01:02:03.887
That will help us narrow down cases.

01:02:03.970 --> 01:02:05.680
Let's try this approach.

01:02:06.598 --> 01:02:09.935
We can focus on the secondary colors,
violet, orange, and green.

01:02:10.018 --> 01:02:13.521
Those narrow down cases to combinations
of white and two different colors.

01:02:13.605 --> 01:02:15.482
You're absolutely right.

01:02:15.565 --> 01:02:19.945
To get the three secondary colors
of violet, orange, and green in Pixel Art,

01:02:20.028 --> 01:02:25.492
the relevant primary colors
must be mixed at a 1-to-1 ratio.

01:02:25.575 --> 01:02:26.868
However,

01:02:26.952 --> 01:02:30.956
you must use three pixel cards
to get the target image.

01:02:31.456 --> 01:02:33.291
As this is the case,

01:02:33.375 --> 01:02:36.628
you will need one white cell
to get the violet cell.

01:02:36.878 --> 01:02:38.296
With secondary colors,

01:02:38.380 --> 01:02:42.217
you need a set like white, red, and blue
or white, red, and yellow.

01:02:42.300 --> 01:02:44.594
I think it's better to use them
to narrow things down.

01:02:45.262 --> 01:02:46.179
- Good idea.
- That way,

01:02:46.263 --> 01:02:47.847
we can easily eliminate a bunch of cards.

01:02:48.848 --> 01:02:50.725
I think I can do a good job
with Pixel Art.

01:02:50.809 --> 01:02:53.937
Rather than looking for three cards
that can give me the target,

01:02:54.020 --> 01:02:56.731
I'll take the target image
and layer it over the cards.

01:02:56.815 --> 01:03:00.902
Ji-min is suggesting a strategy
of placing the target on the cards.

01:03:00.986 --> 01:03:02.404
This way,

01:03:02.487 --> 01:03:06.449
you can eliminate
the unnecessary cards quickly.

01:03:07.617 --> 01:03:11.621
I can weed out irrelevant cards
after comparing them to the target.

01:03:11.705 --> 01:03:13.498
When three cards remain, I have my answer.

01:03:13.581 --> 01:03:16.501
Layering the target over other cards
sounds pretty good.

01:03:17.294 --> 01:03:18.962
Are there any hacks to Time Jump?

01:03:19.045 --> 01:03:20.630
That's the game I'm worried about.

01:03:20.714 --> 01:03:22.716
Why don't we use MOD 30?

01:03:22.799 --> 01:03:23.842
With that...

01:03:23.925 --> 01:03:26.386
Can you give me an example?
It sounds fuzzy to me.

01:03:26.469 --> 01:03:28.513
Let's find out the date
81 days past August 17th.

01:03:28.596 --> 01:03:31.266
Add 81 to 17. We get August 98th.

01:03:31.516 --> 01:03:33.893
- Okay, next?
- Divide 98 by 30.

01:03:33.977 --> 01:03:36.563
- Divide it by 30?
- Then, we get a quotient and a remainder.

01:03:36.896 --> 01:03:39.149
Use the quotient to update the month.

01:03:39.232 --> 01:03:42.068
Then, check how many months with 31 days
come between August and that month.

01:03:42.152 --> 01:03:43.445
- Dock it out?
- Exactly.

01:03:43.528 --> 01:03:45.697
August and October
both have 31 days, right?

01:03:45.780 --> 01:03:47.365
Now, subtract 2 from 8.

01:03:48.283 --> 01:03:50.368
Subtract 2 from 8?
Is the answer November 6th?

01:03:50.452 --> 01:03:51.494
Yes.

01:03:51.578 --> 01:03:53.413
The key is to correctly count
the months with 31 days.

01:03:53.496 --> 01:03:56.082
Make sure to keep that in mind.

01:03:56.374 --> 01:03:58.543
Let's move on to dates.
Ever heard of the Doomsday algorithm?

01:03:58.626 --> 01:04:01.087
- Doomsday algorithm?
- I'll tell you all about it.

01:04:01.171 --> 01:04:03.006
There's this chart

01:04:03.089 --> 01:04:06.760
that lists one day in every month
that occurs on the same day of the week.

01:04:07.010 --> 01:04:08.345
In January, it's the 10th.

01:04:08.428 --> 01:04:10.722
February only has 28 days,
so it's going to be the 28th.

01:04:11.056 --> 01:04:14.851
THE LISTED DATES ALL OCCUR
ON THE SAME DAY OF THE WEEK EVERY YEAR

01:04:14.934 --> 01:04:18.104
Basically, all these days
occur on the same day of the week.

01:04:18.188 --> 01:04:19.189
EXAMPLE
JANUARY 10TH IS A MONDAY

01:04:19.272 --> 01:04:21.941
To find out which day September 7th is,

01:04:22.025 --> 01:04:24.194
you can refer to the Doomsday algorithm

01:04:24.277 --> 01:04:28.656
to learn that January 10th
and September 5th are both Mondays.

01:04:28.740 --> 01:04:31.659
As September 7th
is 2 days past September 5th,

01:04:31.743 --> 01:04:34.704
you can deduce
that September 7th is a Wednesday.

01:04:34.788 --> 01:04:35.997
We can use this information

01:04:36.081 --> 01:04:38.708
to tackle the date questions efficiently.

01:04:38.792 --> 01:04:40.001
When it comes to people,

01:04:40.085 --> 01:04:42.670
focus on noticeable traits
like wearing a headset.

01:04:42.754 --> 01:04:45.298
Here's what I do
when I need to memorize anything.

01:04:45.382 --> 01:04:47.342
Don't try to capture all the details.

01:04:47.425 --> 01:04:51.304
Look at it from afar,
like you're gazing at a forest.

01:04:51.388 --> 01:04:53.556
That way, we can get a general impression.

01:04:53.640 --> 01:04:56.434
But short-term memory
is the key to memorization.

01:04:56.518 --> 01:04:57.644
Hit the buzzer right away.

01:04:57.727 --> 01:04:59.437
- Just go for it.
- That's a must.

01:04:59.521 --> 01:05:00.939
If you miss something, you won't recall.

01:05:01.022 --> 01:05:03.108
You need to at least
win a chance to answer.

01:05:03.191 --> 01:05:04.025
Hands down.

01:05:04.401 --> 01:05:06.236
Which game do you feel most confident in?

01:05:06.694 --> 01:05:08.279
I'll be okay with any of them.

01:05:08.363 --> 01:05:09.656
No, I feel good about all of them.

01:05:09.739 --> 01:05:11.366
This guy has no weaknesses.

01:05:11.449 --> 01:05:12.784
Do you want 2 lives or 3?

01:05:12.992 --> 01:05:14.619
Right, we can give him three lives.

01:05:14.702 --> 01:05:16.830
But three lives might keep people at bay.

01:05:16.913 --> 01:05:19.332
Because they'll see Ji-min
as too big a threat?

01:05:19.416 --> 01:05:21.167
Okay, then. I'll take two lives.

01:05:21.584 --> 01:05:23.086
TEAM KAIST'S LIFE ALLOCATION

01:05:24.337 --> 01:05:25.839
TEAM POSTECH'S LIFE ALLOCATION

01:05:27.048 --> 01:05:28.550
TEAM YONSEI'S LIFE ALLOCATION

01:05:29.717 --> 01:05:33.805
We'll have to win as many points as we can
when we get the initial host position.

01:05:34.013 --> 01:05:36.141
Let's make the most of that perk

01:05:36.224 --> 01:05:38.143
- and win a ton of points.
- We've got to.

01:05:38.226 --> 01:05:39.561
Are you up for it?

01:05:39.644 --> 01:05:41.479
I am, actually.

01:05:41.563 --> 01:05:43.022
Just end it yourself.

01:05:43.106 --> 01:05:45.483
- You can just...
- You want me to win 12 points?

01:05:45.567 --> 01:05:46.943
- Yeah, go ahead.
- I'd love that.

01:05:47.026 --> 01:05:48.361
Don't lose, Ji-min.

01:05:50.405 --> 01:05:52.240
Both teams think we're lightweights.

01:05:52.323 --> 01:05:55.743
They think we're the weaklings,
so they won't try to avoid us.

01:05:55.827 --> 01:06:00.290
I think there's a chance
they won't even let us compete.

01:06:00.373 --> 01:06:02.709
Well, I think that will be to our benefit.

01:06:02.792 --> 01:06:06.171
Let them go head-to-head
and exhaust each other's lives--

01:06:06.254 --> 01:06:08.882
Wait, the lives don't matter.
It's all about points.

01:06:09.174 --> 01:06:11.885
You could even say
lives don't have much of an impact.

01:06:11.968 --> 01:06:13.178
But not the points.

01:06:13.261 --> 01:06:15.305
We must get a chance to compete
and earn points.

01:06:15.388 --> 01:06:17.307
Even if we end up losing,
we've got to compete.

01:06:17.557 --> 01:06:22.228
Let's say Team KAIST goes
after every member of Team POSTECH.

01:06:22.312 --> 01:06:27.275
Team KAIST taking away
Team POSTECH's lives doesn't matter.

01:06:27.358 --> 01:06:30.403
What matters is that they're taking
the points that could have been ours.

01:06:30.487 --> 01:06:31.446
Here's my pitch.

01:06:31.529 --> 01:06:33.823
If Team KAIST selects Team POSTECH
two times in a row,

01:06:33.907 --> 01:06:35.742
we should use the Priority card.

01:06:35.825 --> 01:06:39.746
We'll let them take two points,
but we'll get into the game from Round 3.

01:06:40.872 --> 01:06:44.459
Remember the two guys besides Jun-u,
my opponent in the Deathmatch?

01:06:44.542 --> 01:06:45.835
I think they have a bad memory.

01:06:46.169 --> 01:06:48.213
Oh, I didn't say anything.

01:06:49.380 --> 01:06:53.259
They seem like math and physics prodigies
who are terrible at memorization.

01:06:53.676 --> 01:06:56.387
I think you need to be prepared.

01:06:56.471 --> 01:06:57.514
- Okay.
- Got it?

01:06:57.597 --> 01:07:01.643
There's a high chance
Team KAIST will come after you first.

01:07:01.726 --> 01:07:03.853
Alternatively,
they might go after Team Yonsei.

01:07:03.937 --> 01:07:06.523
They'll remember your performance
from the Deathmatch.

01:07:06.606 --> 01:07:09.567
They've seen you get nervous,
so you'll be high on their target list.

01:07:09.651 --> 01:07:12.445
- I want you to be mentally prepared.
- Okay, I will.

01:07:12.529 --> 01:07:13.988
One more thing.

01:07:14.072 --> 01:07:16.241
Let's say we get picked to compete.

01:07:16.324 --> 01:07:18.993
Then, please remember
that this is a favorable setup for us.

01:07:19.536 --> 01:07:21.371
So be confident

01:07:21.454 --> 01:07:24.290
- and just think about winning, okay?
- Good point.

01:07:24.374 --> 01:07:28.836
If there's any chance
you can control the situation,

01:07:28.920 --> 01:07:30.505
leave Ji-hoo for me.

01:07:30.588 --> 01:07:31.631
I want to take him down.

01:07:31.714 --> 01:07:33.967
LEE JUN-U VOWS TO GET HIS REVENGE
FOR DOUBLE-SIDED BINGO

01:07:34.259 --> 01:07:36.594
Let's not underestimate
Team KAIST and Team POSTECH.

01:07:36.678 --> 01:07:38.096
Yeah, we need to focus.

01:07:38.179 --> 01:07:40.431
There's a chance we might lose,
so let's keep our focus.

01:07:40.515 --> 01:07:42.058
We don't want to regret it later.

01:07:42.141 --> 01:07:45.061
- Think of this as a Deathmatch.
- It is a Deathmatch.

01:07:45.144 --> 01:07:47.689
It's a three-way Deathmatch.

01:07:48.147 --> 01:07:49.190
Let's make it back.

01:07:49.274 --> 01:07:51.484
It's time to awaken the other me.

01:07:51.568 --> 01:07:53.236
I have two souls inside of me.

01:07:53.319 --> 01:07:54.362
Two hearts.

01:07:54.445 --> 01:07:55.405
Yeah, two hearts.

01:07:55.488 --> 01:07:56.406
BOTH HAVE 2 LIVES

01:07:56.489 --> 01:07:58.992
The time for strategy meeting is up.

01:07:59.075 --> 01:08:03.538
All teams, please gather
at the main hall for the match.

01:08:03.871 --> 01:08:06.124
- KAIST!
- Let's go!

01:08:06.207 --> 01:08:07.834
- POSTECH!
- Let's go!

01:08:08.418 --> 01:08:11.087
- Akaraka!
- Let's go, Yonsei!

01:08:19.512 --> 01:08:23.266
We will now begin the redemption round,

01:08:23.349 --> 01:08:26.352
Relay Match.

01:08:26.436 --> 01:08:28.771
- This is going to be fun.
- It will be epic.

01:08:29.022 --> 01:08:31.524
I hope Team KAIST doesn't return.
They're so scary.

01:08:31.608 --> 01:08:34.193
I'd hate to face Ji-min in another game.

01:08:34.277 --> 01:08:36.321
I hope this match will drain them.

01:08:36.988 --> 01:08:41.618
Team KAIST, please announce
which contestant will play as the host.

01:08:42.076 --> 01:08:44.037
I'll be the first host.

01:08:45.079 --> 01:08:47.665
- All right, Ji-min.
- Ji-min.

01:08:47.915 --> 01:08:49.751
He has a thunderous voice.

01:08:49.834 --> 01:08:50.835
He has great energy.

01:08:50.918 --> 01:08:52.879
Yeah, and his energy
can really throw you off.

01:08:52.962 --> 01:08:54.964
He must have nerves of steel.
He's always confident.

01:08:55.048 --> 01:08:58.176
It looks like Ji-min does
all the heavy lifting for Team KAIST.

01:08:58.635 --> 01:09:00.511
He's their Ace player.

01:09:02.055 --> 01:09:07.143
The host, Team KAIST's Jeon Ji-min,
will now select the game.

01:09:07.226 --> 01:09:08.311
6 QUESTIONS EACH

01:09:08.645 --> 01:09:10.563
I wonder what he'll choose.

01:09:11.814 --> 01:09:13.983
I'll go with Pixel Art.

01:09:14.067 --> 01:09:18.071
Team KAIST's Jeon Ji-min
selected Pixel Art.

01:09:18.154 --> 01:09:22.950
Please choose your opponent.

01:09:25.953 --> 01:09:29.123
Team KAIST's priority now
is to find the weakest team.

01:09:29.207 --> 01:09:31.668
I think he'll go with Team POSTECH
because of their rivalry.

01:09:31.751 --> 01:09:33.753
Sure, who can resist a rival match?

01:09:35.171 --> 01:09:39.425
I'll play against
Team POSTECH's Hwang Seok-hun.

01:09:40.510 --> 01:09:43.513
Team KAIST's Jeon Ji-min
chose Team POSTECH's Hwang Seok-hun.

01:09:44.013 --> 01:09:47.058
- Good luck out there. Don't get nervous.
- I won't.

01:09:47.892 --> 01:09:50.311
- It's the first game, so no pressure.
- Good luck.

01:09:51.020 --> 01:09:51.854
You've got this.

01:09:54.440 --> 01:09:57.026
- Let's have a good game.
- Looking forward to it.

01:09:59.278 --> 01:10:02.615
I really hope he'll do well.

01:10:03.825 --> 01:10:05.618
I wanted to repay my friends' trust in me.

01:10:05.702 --> 01:10:09.455
So I tried to empty my mind
and give the game my undivided attention.

01:10:10.206 --> 01:10:14.001
I thought my mission was to stay
as the host as long as I could.

01:10:14.085 --> 01:10:16.003
Basically, I had to win at all costs.

01:10:16.546 --> 01:10:18.464
If Ji-min finishes Team POSTECH off,

01:10:18.548 --> 01:10:20.091
- he can decide the match.
- Absolutely.

01:10:20.174 --> 01:10:22.593
Remember how Team KAIST
shipped Team POSTECH off?

01:10:22.677 --> 01:10:24.178
- In the Deathmatch?
- You're right.

01:10:24.262 --> 01:10:27.557
Those two already had a face-off.

01:10:28.015 --> 01:10:29.934
The first rival match
after the Deathmatch.

01:10:30.017 --> 01:10:31.102
REUNION OF THE OLD RIVALS

01:10:31.185 --> 01:10:33.354
Let us begin Pixel Art.

01:10:33.771 --> 01:10:37.275
THEY MUST SELECT 3 PIXEL CARDS

01:10:43.948 --> 01:10:46.117
- Dang, this is confusing.
- Totally.

01:10:46.200 --> 01:10:48.619
I spotted a promising card,
but I can't find it now.

01:10:55.042 --> 01:10:56.544
Team KAIST's Jeon Ji-min.

01:10:57.003 --> 01:10:58.880
I'll go with Pixel Cards 3, 7, and 8.

01:11:00.214 --> 01:11:01.716
Team KAIST's Jeon Ji-min.

01:11:04.260 --> 01:11:05.428
That is correct.

01:11:07.513 --> 01:11:10.600
PIXEL CARDS 3 AND 7: 180-DEGREE ROTATION

01:11:11.726 --> 01:11:14.020
PERFECT MATCH TO THE TARGET

01:11:15.855 --> 01:11:17.064
How did he get it so quickly?

01:11:17.148 --> 01:11:19.358
- That speed, though.
- How can he solve it so fast?

01:11:19.442 --> 01:11:20.693
You've got to hand it to him.

01:11:20.777 --> 01:11:24.572
Team POSTECH's Hwang Seok-hun.
You lost a life.

01:11:26.199 --> 01:11:27.492
What a shame.

01:11:27.992 --> 01:11:30.161
You still did a great job.

01:11:31.662 --> 01:11:33.748
CURRENT STANDINGS
YONSEI: 0, KAIST: 1, POSTECH: 0

01:11:33.831 --> 01:11:37.376
Team KAIST's Jeon Ji-min.
Please select the next game.

01:11:37.627 --> 01:11:39.253
I'll go with Pixel Art.

01:11:42.131 --> 01:11:45.551
Please choose your opponent.

01:11:45.635 --> 01:11:47.929
It will get wild
if he chooses Seok-hun again.

01:11:49.055 --> 01:11:50.306
That's so hardcore.

01:11:50.389 --> 01:11:52.308
That's the right move
to secure your survival.

01:11:52.892 --> 01:11:54.352
Call Seok-hun again.

01:11:55.853 --> 01:11:57.855
I'll play against Team POSTECH's...

01:11:58.439 --> 01:12:00.775
Team POSTECH's Jae Seung-gyu, please.

01:12:03.152 --> 01:12:05.154
He's targeting people with two lives.

01:12:05.238 --> 01:12:07.073
He's docking everyone's life.

01:12:07.156 --> 01:12:09.033
Looks like he's planning
to wipe out Team POSTECH.

01:12:09.116 --> 01:12:10.827
Here is your question.

01:12:10.910 --> 01:12:13.955
TARGET

01:12:24.465 --> 01:12:25.466
Pixel Card 1's a must, no?

01:12:25.550 --> 01:12:27.343
You need that for the yellow center.

01:12:27.426 --> 01:12:28.344
That's my point.

01:12:31.055 --> 01:12:32.181
Team KAIST's Jeon Ji-min.

01:12:32.598 --> 01:12:35.351
I'll go with Pixel Cards 1, 4, and 7.

01:12:38.104 --> 01:12:39.397
That is correct.

01:12:39.981 --> 01:12:42.108
You will remain as the host.

01:12:43.109 --> 01:12:44.235
Damn it.

01:12:45.236 --> 01:12:49.615
PIXEL CARD 1: 90-DEGREE ROTATION,
PIXEL CARDS 4 AND 7: 180-DEGREE ROTATION

01:12:50.950 --> 01:12:52.118
PERFECT MATCH TO THE TARGET

01:12:52.368 --> 01:12:55.872
Team POSTECH's Jae Seung-gyu lost a life.

01:12:56.247 --> 01:12:57.790
CURRENT STANDINGS
YONSEI: 0, KAIST: 2, POSTECH: 0

01:12:57.874 --> 01:12:59.750
Samsung has a bright future ahead.

01:12:59.834 --> 01:13:00.668
- What?
- Samsung.

01:13:00.751 --> 01:13:02.503
Oh, because he majors
in semiconductor engineering?

01:13:04.088 --> 01:13:05.548
THE FUTURE OF SEMICONDUCTORS IN KOREA

01:13:05.631 --> 01:13:08.301
SEMICONDUCTOR SYSTEM ENGINEERING MAJOR
AND KAIST-SAMSUNG SCHOLARSHIP RECIPIENT

01:13:09.594 --> 01:13:11.804
I'll go with Pixel Art.

01:13:12.430 --> 01:13:13.848
Team KAIST's Jeon Ji-min.

01:13:13.931 --> 01:13:16.934
Please choose your opponent.

01:13:22.899 --> 01:13:24.817
I'll play against
Team POSTECH's Jae Seung-gyu.

01:13:27.945 --> 01:13:30.197
- Didn't he just beat Seung-gyu?
- Yeah.

01:13:31.157 --> 01:13:32.617
That's cruel.

01:13:32.700 --> 01:13:36.787
- Things might get physical after this.
- Looks like it.

01:13:36.871 --> 01:13:41.083
If he keeps on hounding Team POSTECH only,
Team KAIST will make it back.

01:13:41.334 --> 01:13:42.919
That seems to be their game plan.

01:13:43.252 --> 01:13:46.172
Honestly speaking,
I saw Team Yonsei as a bigger threat.

01:13:46.672 --> 01:13:48.925
I think we should target
a single team early on.

01:13:49.008 --> 01:13:52.553
Why don't we strike Team POSTECH
when we have the host position?

01:13:52.637 --> 01:13:54.722
Team POSTECH itself isn't our main target.

01:13:54.805 --> 01:13:57.099
Team Yonsei
will probably target Team POSTECH,

01:13:57.183 --> 01:13:59.435
so we should claim the points
before they can.

01:14:00.061 --> 01:14:01.687
To keep Team Yonsei from winning points?

01:14:01.771 --> 01:14:03.064
Exactly.

01:14:03.898 --> 01:14:06.609
JEON JI-MIN CHOSE
TEAM KAIST CONTESTANTS 3 TIMES IN A ROW

01:14:07.234 --> 01:14:08.444
Let's keep it cool.

01:14:08.527 --> 01:14:10.696
The host, Team KAIST's Jeon Ji-min,

01:14:10.780 --> 01:14:13.783
chose Team KAIST's Jae Seung-gyu
as his opponent.

01:14:14.200 --> 01:14:16.160
Team Yonsei will use the Priority card.

01:14:16.535 --> 01:14:18.663
Team Yonsei will use the Priority card.

01:14:21.248 --> 01:14:22.750
Seung-gyu is being replaced.

01:14:22.959 --> 01:14:26.128
Team Yonsei must've thought
they had to cut in now for survival.

01:14:26.212 --> 01:14:30.675
Team Yonsei's Choi A-in
used the Priority card.

01:14:30.758 --> 01:14:34.011
My team expected to get overlooked
for two rounds.

01:14:34.095 --> 01:14:36.263
That didn't mean
we had to just stand and watch.

01:14:36.347 --> 01:14:38.557
The host will have a new opponent
for this round.

01:14:38.641 --> 01:14:42.228
Team Yonsei's Choi A-in,
please come to the stage.

01:14:42.311 --> 01:14:43.479
Good luck.

01:14:46.273 --> 01:14:47.692
Let's have a good game.

01:14:49.694 --> 01:14:51.737
I saw him beat two opponents back-to-back,

01:14:51.821 --> 01:14:54.407
so I knew he wasn't going
to be an easy mark.

01:14:54.490 --> 01:14:56.742
Still, I didn't let that make me nervous.

01:14:57.702 --> 01:14:58.703
Is it 1, 4, and 7?

01:14:58.786 --> 01:15:00.204
Aren't they the answer?

01:15:00.287 --> 01:15:01.831
A-IN SOLVED THE PREVIOUS QUESTION
FASTER THAN JI-MIN

01:15:02.665 --> 01:15:04.000
I want to volunteer.

01:15:05.084 --> 01:15:08.170
I told myself, "He may be good,
but not overwhelmingly good."

01:15:08.462 --> 01:15:10.131
I was actually expecting

01:15:10.214 --> 01:15:12.633
that they would make a move
to take the host position.

01:15:12.717 --> 01:15:15.553
A-in is a strong contender
with good results in the pre-test,

01:15:15.803 --> 01:15:17.930
so I tensed up a bit.

01:15:18.764 --> 01:15:20.474
Here is your question.

01:15:21.308 --> 01:15:24.520
TARGET

01:15:33.279 --> 01:15:36.240
Do they need yellow and red to get orange?

01:15:36.323 --> 01:15:37.199
Yes.

01:15:37.742 --> 01:15:39.410
They'll need Pixel Card 9.

01:15:46.083 --> 01:15:48.377
I'll go with Pixel Cards 4, 7...

01:15:50.504 --> 01:15:51.630
and 6.

01:15:56.802 --> 01:15:59.180
Team KAIST's Jeon Ji-min.
That is incorrect.

01:16:01.223 --> 01:16:04.143
PIXEL CARDS 4, 6, 7: WRONG COMBINATION

01:16:04.226 --> 01:16:06.062
Come on, A-in.

01:16:08.522 --> 01:16:10.024
Team Yonsei's Choi A-in.

01:16:10.608 --> 01:16:12.735
I'll go with Pixel Cards 2, 4, and 9.

01:16:17.698 --> 01:16:20.284
Team Yonsei's Choi A-in. That is correct.

01:16:24.080 --> 01:16:26.749
I failed to win
as many points as I could as the host,

01:16:26.832 --> 01:16:27.833
so that was disappointing.

01:16:27.917 --> 01:16:29.585
- She took it from him.
- She did it.

01:16:29.668 --> 01:16:31.837
- I got so nervous just now.
- Same here.

01:16:32.713 --> 01:16:34.965
So Ji-min went down?

01:16:36.592 --> 01:16:41.097
PIXEL CARD 2: 180-DEGREE ROTATION
PIXEL CARDS 4 AND 9: 90-DEGREE ROTATION

01:16:41.680 --> 01:16:43.599
PERFECT MATCH TO THE TARGET

01:16:43.849 --> 01:16:47.061
Team Yonsei's Choi A-in is the new host.

01:16:47.144 --> 01:16:49.522
It was satisfying
to contribute to my team.

01:16:49.605 --> 01:16:54.151
It gave me hope that I could lead
my team to victory and survival.

01:16:54.819 --> 01:16:56.112
Such a shame.

01:16:58.697 --> 01:17:00.449
CURRENT STANDINGS
YONSEI: 1, KAIST: 2, POSTECH: 0

01:17:00.533 --> 01:17:01.575
Did I win two points?

01:17:02.076 --> 01:17:03.119
I wasn't concerned before,

01:17:03.202 --> 01:17:05.287
but I started to worry
that things might go down

01:17:05.371 --> 01:17:07.373
after my initial loss.

01:17:07.748 --> 01:17:08.916
How do we proceed?

01:17:08.999 --> 01:17:10.793
I think we can wait it out.

01:17:11.252 --> 01:17:14.004
She may choose one of us.

01:17:14.421 --> 01:17:18.134
Team Yonsei's Choi A-in.
Please select the next game.

01:17:18.551 --> 01:17:20.886
I'll go with Pixel Art.

01:17:20.970 --> 01:17:24.640
Please choose your opponent.

01:17:26.308 --> 01:17:29.562
I thought I had to choose someone
I could certainly defeat.

01:17:33.274 --> 01:17:35.860
You think she's looking at me?
Maybe it's you.

01:17:41.323 --> 01:17:42.825
Will she choose Team POSTECH, too?

01:17:42.908 --> 01:17:45.452
- I won't blame them if they get offended.
- Me neither.

01:17:45.536 --> 01:17:48.914
- She has to do what's best for her team.
- Yeah, that's true.

01:17:49.123 --> 01:17:51.667
CHOI A-IN WALKS UP TO TEAM POSTECH

01:17:52.084 --> 01:17:54.044
Do I have any volunteers?

01:17:54.336 --> 01:17:55.796
Do I have any volunteers?

01:18:00.092 --> 01:18:02.303
When provoked, people tend to tense up.

01:18:02.386 --> 01:18:05.431
I was hoping to intimidate them
with my surprise question.

01:18:07.224 --> 01:18:09.685
I choose Team POSTECH's Jae Seung-gyu
as my opponent.

01:18:10.019 --> 01:18:13.147
- Okay, I'll see you later.
- Focus, okay? She's not so fast.

01:18:13.230 --> 01:18:16.942
HOST: TEAM YONSEI, CHOI A-IN
OPPONENT: TEAM POSTECH, JAE SEUNG-GYU

01:18:17.234 --> 01:18:18.485
That should make him mad.

01:18:18.569 --> 01:18:19.570
WHY?

01:18:19.653 --> 01:18:21.113
He got selected three times.

01:18:21.197 --> 01:18:23.073
I was chosen three times in a row.

01:18:23.157 --> 01:18:25.326
That didn't make me feel great, exactly.

01:18:25.409 --> 01:18:27.203
It fueled my drive to win.

01:18:27.953 --> 01:18:29.496
Here is your question.

01:18:29.830 --> 01:18:33.000
TARGET

01:18:34.418 --> 01:18:35.794
This one is difficult.

01:18:35.878 --> 01:18:37.546
It's gotten much harder.

01:18:37.630 --> 01:18:39.840
We had more empty cells in earlier rounds.

01:18:58.484 --> 01:18:59.652
So soon?

01:18:59.735 --> 01:19:01.695
Wow, he has a lot of fight left in him.

01:19:01.904 --> 01:19:03.864
I'll go with Pixel Cards 4, 5, and 9.

01:19:05.783 --> 01:19:08.619
PIXEL CARDS 4, 5, 9: WRONG COMBINATION

01:19:08.702 --> 01:19:11.580
Team POSTECH's Jae Seung-gyu.
That is incorrect.

01:19:11.664 --> 01:19:14.124
Your opponent will now get
the chance to answer.

01:19:14.583 --> 01:19:16.418
Why is my heart racing?

01:19:21.507 --> 01:19:22.925
You have five seconds left.

01:19:24.510 --> 01:19:27.054
Come on.

01:19:29.431 --> 01:19:30.391
Ten seconds have passed.

01:19:30.474 --> 01:19:33.727
OPEN FLOOR AFTER 10 SECONDS
Both contestants are allowed to answer.

01:19:33.811 --> 01:19:35.354
Please help us out, Seung-gyu.

01:19:39.483 --> 01:19:41.360
I'll go with Pixel Cards 1, 5, and 9.

01:19:42.027 --> 01:19:43.529
Team POSTECH's Jae Seung-gyu.

01:19:47.658 --> 01:19:48.784
That is correct.

01:19:50.536 --> 01:19:54.415
PIXEL CARD 1: 90-DEGREE ROTATION,
PIXEL CARDS 5 AND 9: 180-DEGREE ROTATION

01:19:55.416 --> 01:19:56.375
PERFECT MATCH TO THE TARGET

01:19:56.458 --> 01:19:57.459
That is correct.

01:19:58.585 --> 01:20:02.172
Team POSTECH's Jae Seung-gyu
is the new host.

01:20:02.631 --> 01:20:03.716
It felt amazing.

01:20:03.799 --> 01:20:06.719
I finally got the chance
to show everyone my worth.

01:20:06.802 --> 01:20:09.888
Team Yonsei used the Priority card,
but they only earned a single point.

01:20:09.972 --> 01:20:11.265
They're in big trouble.

01:20:11.598 --> 01:20:14.226
Team Yonsei's Choi A-in lost a life.

01:20:14.310 --> 01:20:16.270
Please return to your place.

01:20:20.065 --> 01:20:21.817
CURRENT STANDINGS
YONSEI: 1, KAIST: 2, POSTECH: 1

01:20:21.900 --> 01:20:23.902
The host, Team POSTECH's Jae Seung-gyu,

01:20:23.986 --> 01:20:25.779
will now select the next game.

01:20:26.155 --> 01:20:27.906
I'll go with Time Jump.

01:20:28.157 --> 01:20:30.409
I'm so curious. I wanted to try that one.

01:20:30.492 --> 01:20:32.036
All right. Time Jump!

01:20:32.119 --> 01:20:33.537
I can't wait.

01:20:33.996 --> 01:20:35.414
Good.

01:20:35.497 --> 01:20:38.500
Please choose your opponent.

01:20:42.838 --> 01:20:46.800
I wanted to get back on stage,
beat him, and reclaim the host role.

01:20:47.468 --> 01:20:49.011
I wonder who he'll choose.

01:20:50.054 --> 01:20:52.097
CHOOSE SOMEONE FROM TEAM KAIST

01:20:52.598 --> 01:20:56.060
HAND SIGNAL RECEIVED

01:20:58.312 --> 01:21:00.356
I'll play against Team KAIST's Kim Ji-u.

01:21:00.814 --> 01:21:03.192
Team KAIST's Kim Ji-u,
please come to the stage.

01:21:08.739 --> 01:21:10.240
Here's your question.

01:21:11.367 --> 01:21:12.618
USE NUMBERS FROM 1 TO 6

01:21:12.701 --> 01:21:16.997
(2-DIGIT) MINUTES PAST (1-DIGIT):(1-DIGIT)
IS (1-DIGIT):(1-DIGIT)

01:21:20.709 --> 01:21:22.378
Team POSTECH's Jae Seung-gyu.

01:21:22.461 --> 01:21:24.380
- Already?
- He has an answer already?

01:21:25.255 --> 01:21:27.007
- So quick.
- He's so fast.

01:21:27.257 --> 01:21:28.759
Please state your answer.

01:21:29.927 --> 01:21:34.848
The answer is,
62 minutes past 4:01 is 5:03.

01:21:36.141 --> 01:21:38.477
Team POSTECH's Jae Seung-gyu.
That is correct.

01:21:42.731 --> 01:21:45.150
Is this the beginning
of a new king's reign?

01:21:45.567 --> 01:21:47.152
I hope Team POSTECH crushes them.

01:21:47.236 --> 01:21:51.490
- A shot at Team Yonsei...
- A shot at Team KAIST. Bang, bang.

01:21:51.740 --> 01:21:54.159
CURRENT STANDINGS
YONSEI: 1, KAIST: 2, POSTECH: 2

01:21:54.368 --> 01:21:57.746
Team POSTECH's Jae Seung-gyu.
Please select the next game.

01:21:58.414 --> 01:22:00.999
I'll go with Time Jump.

01:22:01.208 --> 01:22:03.502
Please choose your opponent.

01:22:04.711 --> 01:22:05.921
Why don't you choose me?

01:22:06.630 --> 01:22:08.465
Why don't you choose me?

01:22:08.549 --> 01:22:11.051
Should I raise my hand?

01:22:17.141 --> 01:22:18.642
Go with Team KAIST one more time.

01:22:19.309 --> 01:22:22.062
Because we had seen
Team Yonsei playing an active role

01:22:22.146 --> 01:22:23.814
in preparing strategies
for Mine and Trade,

01:22:23.897 --> 01:22:26.400
we determined that
they would be harder to defeat.

01:22:26.483 --> 01:22:30.737
That's why we decided
to target Team KAIST instead.

01:22:31.238 --> 01:22:32.156
HOST: TEAM POSTECH, JAE SEUNG-GYU

01:22:32.239 --> 01:22:34.450
I'll play against
Team KAIST's Kang Ji-hoo.

01:22:35.617 --> 01:22:36.827
- This isn't good.
- Who did he want?

01:22:36.910 --> 01:22:38.287
Someone from Team KAIST.

01:22:39.455 --> 01:22:41.248
Let us begin Time Jump.

01:22:41.331 --> 01:22:43.208
Here is your question.

01:22:43.292 --> 01:22:45.002
USE NUMBERS FROM 1 TO 7

01:22:45.085 --> 01:22:50.132
(2-DIGIT) MINUTES PAST (1-DIGIT):(1-DIGIT)
IS (1-DIGIT):(2-DIGIT)

01:23:12.112 --> 01:23:13.572
That startled me.

01:23:19.036 --> 01:23:19.995
Seventy...

01:23:22.789 --> 01:23:26.585
My mind went blank after I blurted out 70.
I couldn't recall the answer.

01:23:26.668 --> 01:23:29.046
Your opponent will now get
the chance to answer.

01:23:29.129 --> 01:23:30.631
TEAM POSTECH CAN ANSWER NOW

01:23:30.714 --> 01:23:32.132
Team POSTECH's Jae Seung-gyu.

01:23:32.216 --> 01:23:37.304
The answer is,
76 minutes past 3:05 is 4:21.

01:23:37.638 --> 01:23:40.098
Team POSTECH's Jae Seung-gyu.
That is correct.

01:23:41.058 --> 01:23:41.892
He's good.

01:23:42.476 --> 01:23:45.395
- He's really good.
- Seung-gyu is on fire.

01:23:45.979 --> 01:23:49.107
Team POSTECH's Jae Seung-gyu
will remain as the host.

01:23:49.483 --> 01:23:51.401
The new king's reign has begun.

01:23:51.485 --> 01:23:54.613
Now, I don't even want Team POSTECH.
Why are they all so good?

01:23:54.696 --> 01:23:57.491
I wish the winner didn't have to join us.

01:23:57.574 --> 01:23:59.910
I hope the creators
will scrap the redemption round.

01:23:59.993 --> 01:24:02.871
Seung-gyu has won
three consecutive rounds.

01:24:03.205 --> 01:24:04.248
Team KAIST's Kang Ji-hoo.

01:24:04.331 --> 01:24:07.584
You don't have any life left
and cannot compete anymore.

01:24:07.668 --> 01:24:08.669
Please leave the main hall.

01:24:08.752 --> 01:24:11.088
- Good luck, guys.
- We'll do our best.

01:24:12.339 --> 01:24:13.882
It was very upsetting.

01:24:13.966 --> 01:24:17.469
I felt terrible that I failed
to help secure our team's survival.

01:24:18.804 --> 01:24:20.764
CURRENT STANDINGS
YONSEI: 1, KAIST: 2, POSTECH: 3

01:24:20.847 --> 01:24:23.183
Please select the next game.

01:24:24.059 --> 01:24:25.477
I'll go with Time Jump.

01:24:26.144 --> 01:24:27.187
Who will he choose next?

01:24:27.563 --> 01:24:28.981
He'll choose one of us now.

01:24:33.485 --> 01:24:35.028
HOST: TEAM POSTECH, JAE SEUNG-GYU

01:24:35.112 --> 01:24:37.239
I'll play against
Team KAIST's Kim Jae-han.

01:24:38.365 --> 01:24:40.033
Team KAIST again?

01:24:41.994 --> 01:24:44.246
- He chose Jae-han.
- He's out to crush them one by one.

01:24:44.329 --> 01:24:46.456
- Seung-gyu's good.
- I'm enjoying this.

01:24:49.668 --> 01:24:52.254
Okay. You've got this, Jae-han.

01:24:52.504 --> 01:24:54.131
Let us begin Time Jump.

01:24:54.214 --> 01:24:55.716
Here is your question.

01:24:55.799 --> 01:24:57.050
USE NUMBERS FROM 0 TO 7

01:24:59.386 --> 01:25:01.096
They need a three-digit number?

01:25:01.513 --> 01:25:03.223
(3-DIGIT) MINUTES PAST (1-DIGIT):(2-DIGIT)
IS (1-DIGIT):(1-DIGIT)

01:25:03.307 --> 01:25:04.266
What?

01:25:04.975 --> 01:25:05.809
Are you serious?

01:25:05.892 --> 01:25:09.730
(3-DIGIT) MINUTES PAST (1-DIGIT):(2-DIGIT)
IS (1-DIGIT):(1-DIGIT)

01:25:09.813 --> 01:25:14.067
NOTE: DON'T USE 0 FOR THE HOUR

01:25:14.318 --> 01:25:16.778
Zero has to go in the middle
of the three-digit number.

01:25:16.862 --> 01:25:18.238
It can't go anywhere else.

01:25:18.322 --> 01:25:20.532
So the 3-digit number must be
in the 100s or the 200s.

01:25:20.616 --> 01:25:22.784
I'd say it's in the 200s.

01:25:27.581 --> 01:25:30.459
I thought,
"I'm so screwed. It's all over."

01:25:30.542 --> 01:25:32.336
Please...

01:25:32.502 --> 01:25:35.797
The answer is,
206 minutes past 4:35 is 7:01.

01:25:36.548 --> 01:25:38.342
Team POSTECH's Jae Seung-gyu.

01:25:40.385 --> 01:25:41.970
206 MINUTES PAST 4:35 IS 7:01

01:25:42.054 --> 01:25:43.055
That is incorrect.

01:25:43.138 --> 01:25:45.390
Your opponent will now get
the chance to answer.

01:25:49.227 --> 01:25:51.521
You've got this, Jae-han. Take your shot.

01:25:51.730 --> 01:25:53.106
You have five seconds left.

01:25:55.317 --> 01:25:56.485
Ten seconds have passed.

01:25:56.568 --> 01:25:59.363
Both contestants are allowed to answer.

01:26:01.406 --> 01:26:02.658
Team KAIST's Kim Jae-han.

01:26:02.949 --> 01:26:08.080
The answer is,
205 minutes past 3:41 is 7:06.

01:26:12.668 --> 01:26:15.212
Team KAIST's Kim Jae-han. That is correct.

01:26:19.383 --> 01:26:23.178
Team KAIST's Kim Jae-han is the new host.

01:26:24.930 --> 01:26:26.556
This changes everything.

01:26:26.640 --> 01:26:28.642
That means Seung-gyu is out of life, no?

01:26:28.725 --> 01:26:31.728
Team POSTECH's Jae Seung-gyu.
You don't have any life left

01:26:32.270 --> 01:26:34.314
and cannot compete anymore.

01:26:34.398 --> 01:26:35.774
Please leave the main hall.

01:26:37.067 --> 01:26:39.986
REMAINING LIFE COUNT
TEAM POSTECH, JAE SEUNG-GYU: 0

01:26:40.320 --> 01:26:42.114
CURRENT STANDINGS
YONSEI: 1, KAIST: 3, POSTECH: 3

01:26:42.447 --> 01:26:46.743
The host, Team KAIST's Kim Jae-han,
will now select the next game.

01:26:46.827 --> 01:26:48.286
I'll go with Time Jump.

01:26:48.995 --> 01:26:51.998
Please choose your opponent.

01:27:00.674 --> 01:27:03.051
Excuse me, Jae-han.

01:27:03.427 --> 01:27:05.887
Why don't you choose one of us?
Come on, we're game.

01:27:06.263 --> 01:27:08.306
I couldn't just stand there.
I had to do something.

01:27:08.390 --> 01:27:09.766
So I threw down the gauntlet.

01:27:16.857 --> 01:27:17.941
I'll play against...

01:27:18.525 --> 01:27:20.819
I'll play against Park Seo-yeon.

01:27:20.902 --> 01:27:23.113
Targeting one team
is the right strategy here.

01:27:23.363 --> 01:27:25.741
- I knew he'd go with Team POSTECH.
- He had to.

01:27:25.824 --> 01:27:27.367
He needs to be strategic.

01:27:27.451 --> 01:27:30.620
Team Yonsei made a big blunder,
using the Priority card too soon.

01:27:30.954 --> 01:27:32.497
They should've saved it.

01:27:32.956 --> 01:27:35.709
I should've held on to the host position.

01:27:35.792 --> 01:27:38.336
I'm sorry
I didn't get to keep it for long.

01:27:38.420 --> 01:27:39.421
It's okay.

01:27:40.046 --> 01:27:41.548
- Hello.
- Hello.

01:27:43.300 --> 01:27:44.926
Here's your question.

01:27:45.010 --> 01:27:46.428
USE NUMBERS FROM 0 TO 5

01:27:46.511 --> 01:27:48.722
THE NEW QUESTION INVOLVES DATES

01:27:48.805 --> 01:27:50.265
Finally.

01:27:50.515 --> 01:27:52.058
We've got dates now?

01:27:52.142 --> 01:27:55.479
(2-DIGIT) DAYS PAST (1-DIGIT)/(1-DIGIT)
IS (1-DIGIT)/(1-DIGIT)

01:27:55.562 --> 01:27:59.274
NOTE: FEBRUARY ALWAYS HAS 28 DAYS

01:27:59.566 --> 01:28:00.984
Where do we put the zero?

01:28:01.067 --> 01:28:04.529
It can only go into the second digit
in the two-digit number, right?

01:28:04.613 --> 01:28:07.491
Okay, then. That means
the first month is an odd month.

01:28:10.786 --> 01:28:12.204
Team KAIST's Kim Jae-han.

01:28:12.579 --> 01:28:15.373
The answer is,
30 days past January 5th is February 4th.

01:28:15.457 --> 01:28:17.709
Team KAIST's Kim Jae-han. That is correct.

01:28:17.793 --> 01:28:19.628
You will remain as the host.

01:28:20.295 --> 01:28:22.756
TEAM POSTECH'S PARK SEO-YEON IS ELIMINATED

01:28:22.839 --> 01:28:24.758
CURRENT STANDINGS
YONSEI: 1, KAIST: 4, POSTECH: 3

01:28:25.550 --> 01:28:29.721
The host, Team KAIST's Kim Jae-han,
will now select the next game.

01:28:30.263 --> 01:28:31.640
I'll go with Pixel Art.

01:28:32.140 --> 01:28:35.769
Team KAIST's Kim Jae-han
selected Pixel Art.

01:28:35.852 --> 01:28:38.772
Please choose your opponent.

01:28:40.357 --> 01:28:42.317
It's time to end Team POSTECH.

01:28:50.617 --> 01:28:52.244
HOST: TEAM KAIST, KIM JAE-HAN

01:28:52.327 --> 01:28:53.995
I'll play against Hwang Seok-hun.

01:28:54.079 --> 01:28:55.121
Oh, man.

01:28:55.205 --> 01:28:56.206
- Take your time.
- Okay.

01:28:56.289 --> 01:28:59.167
- Don't worry about getting it wrong.
- Okay.

01:29:00.544 --> 01:29:04.965
Wow, so smart.
We saw him flounder with Pixel Art.

01:29:05.048 --> 01:29:06.925
Jae-han is amazing.

01:29:07.175 --> 01:29:10.095
If Seok-hun wins this round
and Jun-u wins most of Photo Memory,

01:29:10.178 --> 01:29:12.556
we have a good chance of survival.

01:29:12.639 --> 01:29:15.559
Team POSTECH's Hwang Seok-hun,
please come to the stage.

01:29:15.642 --> 01:29:17.477
Don't freeze up. Go get him.

01:29:19.646 --> 01:29:23.149
I realized that I could wrap things up
if I could beat two POSTECH contestants.

01:29:23.650 --> 01:29:25.277
That didn't seem like a huge challenge,

01:29:25.360 --> 01:29:28.196
so I set my mind
on taking them down one by one.

01:29:28.822 --> 01:29:30.907
- It's a rematch of their Deathmatch.
- That's true.

01:29:30.991 --> 01:29:31.825
REUNION AFTER DOUBLE-SIDED BINGO

01:29:32.492 --> 01:29:36.246
Team KAIST's Kim Jae-han
got a bingo first.

01:29:36.329 --> 01:29:38.790
KIM JAE-HAN DEFEATED HWANG SEOK-HUN

01:29:40.041 --> 01:29:41.668
We need Seok-hun to win.

01:29:41.877 --> 01:29:44.421
I hope Seok-hun will surprise all of us.

01:29:44.880 --> 01:29:47.924
I wanted to secure a win no matter what.

01:29:48.008 --> 01:29:49.509
Here is your question.

01:29:49.885 --> 01:29:53.763
TARGET

01:29:59.352 --> 01:30:01.521
Do your thing, Jae-han.
You were the best in this.

01:30:01.605 --> 01:30:04.107
He beat all of us in practice runs.

01:30:05.483 --> 01:30:07.611
Jeez, what a headache.

01:30:09.154 --> 01:30:11.489
I'm completely lost this time.

01:30:12.115 --> 01:30:14.242
It might be easier
to focus on primary colors.

01:30:14.326 --> 01:30:15.785
It's the fastest to sort out the cards

01:30:15.869 --> 01:30:19.331
based on the primary colors,
then the secondary colors on the sides.

01:30:20.290 --> 01:30:21.374
That's a solid idea.

01:30:27.547 --> 01:30:29.007
Team POSTECH's Hwang Seok-hun.

01:30:29.090 --> 01:30:31.635
I'll go with Pixel Cards 3, 4, and 6.

01:30:32.427 --> 01:30:34.095
Please be right.

01:30:34.471 --> 01:30:36.514
He sounded so sure of his answer.

01:30:39.351 --> 01:30:41.144
Team POSTECH's Hwang Seok-hun.

01:30:43.146 --> 01:30:44.189
That is incorrect.

01:30:44.272 --> 01:30:46.608
Your opponent will now get
the chance to answer.

01:30:46.691 --> 01:30:48.318
That's a bummer.

01:30:48.401 --> 01:30:50.570
This game is harder than it looks.

01:30:50.654 --> 01:30:53.323
Plus, your mind goes blank
when you're out there.

01:30:57.786 --> 01:30:59.037
Team KAIST's Kim Jae-han.

01:30:59.204 --> 01:31:01.081
I'll go with Pixel Cards 2, 4, and 6.

01:31:05.835 --> 01:31:08.088
Team KAIST's Kim Jae-han. That is correct.

01:31:10.757 --> 01:31:12.092
PIXEL CARD 2: 180-DEGREE ROTATION

01:31:12.175 --> 01:31:14.719
PIXEL CARD 4: 270-DEGREE ROTATION,
PIXEL CARD 6: 90-DEGREE ROTATION

01:31:15.637 --> 01:31:17.973
PERFECT MATCH TO THE TARGET

01:31:18.515 --> 01:31:19.641
I can't believe this.

01:31:19.724 --> 01:31:21.810
- He's so good.
- He really is.

01:31:21.893 --> 01:31:23.269
He's killing it.

01:31:24.187 --> 01:31:25.647
- Jae-han won.
- He won again.

01:31:25.730 --> 01:31:27.315
Team KAIST is likely to make it back.

01:31:27.399 --> 01:31:28.817
We're so close, though.

01:31:28.900 --> 01:31:31.444
If only we could beat Team KAIST...

01:31:31.528 --> 01:31:34.072
- But we only have Jun-u now.
- That's true.

01:31:38.994 --> 01:31:40.328
Team POSTECH's Hwang Seok-hun.

01:31:40.412 --> 01:31:43.748
You don't have any life left
and cannot compete anymore.

01:31:43.832 --> 01:31:45.250
Please leave the main hall.

01:31:45.875 --> 01:31:47.460
Wow, he's an absolute genius.

01:31:47.544 --> 01:31:49.254
How many games has he won now?

01:31:51.464 --> 01:31:54.718
KIM JAE-HAN HAS WON 3 CONSECUTIVE GAMES

01:31:55.051 --> 01:31:56.845
CURRENT STANDINGS
YONSEI: 1, KAIST: 5, POSTECH: 3

01:31:57.053 --> 01:31:59.472
This round can be
Team POSTECH's last one, right?

01:31:59.556 --> 01:32:00.515
Yeah.

01:32:00.598 --> 01:32:02.892
But if Jun-u wins three rounds,
he can turn the tables.

01:32:02.976 --> 01:32:04.019
Jun-u is the calm type, so--

01:32:04.102 --> 01:32:06.104
- But if he loses, we're done.
- Well, I suppose.

01:32:06.187 --> 01:32:08.148
Then, we're really out of the game.

01:32:08.440 --> 01:32:11.026
TEAM POSTECH'S LAST SURVIVOR, LEE JUN-U

01:32:11.109 --> 01:32:13.361
Please select the next game.

01:32:13.987 --> 01:32:15.405
I'll go with Pixel Art.

01:32:16.990 --> 01:32:19.909
Please choose your opponent.

01:32:20.910 --> 01:32:24.039
Eliminate Jun-u, and we're done.
It's all over.

01:32:24.581 --> 01:32:26.374
I'll play against Lee Jun-u.

01:32:27.000 --> 01:32:30.378
Team POSTECH's Lee Jun-u,
please come to the stage.

01:32:32.422 --> 01:32:35.300
I told myself if I took my time
and reviewed cards at my own pace,

01:32:35.383 --> 01:32:37.302
then I'd be able to defeat Jae-han.

01:32:40.180 --> 01:32:42.849
You can do this, Jae-han.

01:32:42.932 --> 01:32:44.309
You're that good.

01:32:45.393 --> 01:32:48.229
Please come through for us, Jun-u.

01:32:48.313 --> 01:32:50.106
Let us begin Pixel Art.

01:32:50.190 --> 01:32:51.900
Here is your question.

01:32:52.192 --> 01:32:55.111
TARGET

01:33:02.118 --> 01:33:03.953
This is super challenging.

01:33:04.037 --> 01:33:05.914
Dang, it's making me dizzy.

01:33:08.708 --> 01:33:09.918
Team KAIST's Kim Jae-han.

01:33:10.251 --> 01:33:11.711
Oh, what?

01:33:11.795 --> 01:33:13.171
How is he pulling it off?

01:33:13.254 --> 01:33:14.714
- He's so fast.
- Definitely.

01:33:15.090 --> 01:33:17.008
I'll go with Pixel Cards 1, 3, and 9.

01:33:18.510 --> 01:33:19.719
I can't bear to watch.

01:33:21.471 --> 01:33:23.264
Oh, please...

01:33:23.348 --> 01:33:24.724
Pretty please...

01:33:24.808 --> 01:33:27.060
Team KAIST's Kim Jae-han. That is correct.

01:33:28.853 --> 01:33:31.231
PIXEL CARD 1: 180-DEGREE ROTATION,
PIXEL CARDS 3 AND 9: 270-DEGREE ROTATION

01:33:32.232 --> 01:33:33.983
PERFECT MATCH TO THE TARGET

01:33:36.361 --> 01:33:42.075
Even if Team Yonsei managed
to defeat the remaining Team KAIST,

01:33:42.158 --> 01:33:45.120
their total score
would only amount to four points.

01:33:45.203 --> 01:33:49.499
As such, we will apply the mercy rule
and end the game.

01:33:50.083 --> 01:33:52.168
- Oh, shoot.
- It's over.

01:33:53.169 --> 01:33:54.295
How disappointing.

01:33:54.379 --> 01:33:56.881
If only I had gotten
that Time Jump question right.

01:33:56.965 --> 01:33:58.091
I'm sorry.

01:33:58.925 --> 01:34:00.927
I shouldn't have chosen Jae-han.

01:34:01.928 --> 01:34:03.638
Oh, Team KAIST's back in the game.

01:34:03.847 --> 01:34:04.889
Damn it.

01:34:05.557 --> 01:34:07.934
We went full savage
to get them eliminated, but...

01:34:09.435 --> 01:34:11.563
Thank you for the good game.

01:34:13.565 --> 01:34:16.860
- He beat four people all by himself.
- He's amazing.

01:34:16.943 --> 01:34:19.195
How is this real?

01:34:19.696 --> 01:34:23.783
KIM JAE-HAN ELIMINATED
ALL 4 CONTESTANTS OF TEAM POSTECH

01:34:23.867 --> 01:34:26.286
That was a major boost to my confidence.

01:34:26.578 --> 01:34:29.330
I thought I could contribute more

01:34:29.414 --> 01:34:32.625
if I took on a more active role
in the upcoming games.

01:34:32.709 --> 01:34:35.879
I'll take this
as a fresh shot at Elite League

01:34:35.962 --> 01:34:37.338
and do my absolute best.

01:34:44.137 --> 01:34:47.015
I felt disappointed in myself.

01:34:47.348 --> 01:34:49.434
If only I had hit the buzzer
faster than Seung-gyu,

01:34:49.517 --> 01:34:51.895
I could've stayed on as the host.

01:34:51.978 --> 01:34:54.564
Looking back,
I realize I might have been too impatient.

01:34:54.647 --> 01:34:56.941
I felt bad for my teammates, too.

01:34:57.025 --> 01:34:59.319
Then again,
every good redemption round is brutal.

01:34:59.402 --> 01:35:02.488
The winner gets a new shot.
We need some cruelty.

01:35:02.780 --> 01:35:04.032
It was a fair game.

01:35:04.115 --> 01:35:06.034
All teams were given the Priority card.

01:35:06.117 --> 01:35:08.995
Team Yonsei should've saved it

01:35:09.537 --> 01:35:11.998
so they could use it
when they knew they wouldn't lose.

01:35:12.081 --> 01:35:13.291
- They used it too early.
- Right.

01:35:13.374 --> 01:35:14.792
Now that it's come to this,

01:35:14.876 --> 01:35:17.837
you could say Team KAIST proved
that they're better than these two.

01:35:17.921 --> 01:35:21.090
Team KAIST went through two Deathmatches
and the redemption round.

01:35:21.174 --> 01:35:22.550
They really made it back from hell.

01:35:22.634 --> 01:35:25.303
That makes them more formidable
than Team KAIST of Season 2.

01:35:30.683 --> 01:35:33.019
This was an opportunity
none of us expected.

01:35:33.102 --> 01:35:36.522
We never imagined
that we could return to this hall again.

01:35:36.981 --> 01:35:38.608
I wanted to try Photo Memory, though.

01:35:38.691 --> 01:35:41.069
Same here.
It's a shame we never got to compete.

01:35:43.738 --> 01:35:48.326
That concludes the redemption round,
Relay Match.

01:35:48.660 --> 01:35:50.995
Now, the final results.

01:35:51.079 --> 01:35:56.584
As Team KAIST obtained the most points,
Team KAIST won the match.

01:35:59.837 --> 01:36:03.591
As the winner of the redemption round,
Team KAIST secured a second chance.

01:36:03.675 --> 01:36:07.804
They can rejoin the surviving teams
and compete in Elite League Season 3.

01:36:08.721 --> 01:36:10.598
Thank you.

01:36:11.349 --> 01:36:15.270
Team Yonsei and Team POSTECH,
you failed to secure a second chance.

01:36:15.353 --> 01:36:17.063
Please exit the grounds.

01:36:21.317 --> 01:36:22.652
Good luck, guys.

01:36:30.118 --> 01:36:30.952
Good job.

01:36:31.244 --> 01:36:32.787
We're hard to get rid of.

01:36:32.870 --> 01:36:34.372
We keep coming back.

01:36:35.206 --> 01:36:36.499
We went through two Deathmatches

01:36:36.582 --> 01:36:39.210
and barely managed
to win the redemption round.

01:36:39.377 --> 01:36:42.588
Now that we're back,
we really should aim for the trophy.

01:36:51.931 --> 01:36:55.226
Today's main match is Dilemma of the Mean.

01:36:55.310 --> 01:36:56.144
What?

01:36:56.352 --> 01:36:57.186
Dilemma?

01:36:57.270 --> 01:36:58.813
- Sounds like a mind game.
- It's a mind game.

01:37:00.523 --> 01:37:03.609
Let's make ourselves untouchable
and let the rest fight it out.

01:37:03.693 --> 01:37:04.986
I do feel nervous.

01:37:05.069 --> 01:37:07.196
Team KAIST made it back from hell twice.

01:37:07.280 --> 01:37:08.364
Is it a revenge match?

01:37:08.448 --> 01:37:10.658
Like, "We're back from the dead"?

01:37:10.742 --> 01:37:13.911
We should've tried to get
in Team KAIST's good books.

01:37:13.995 --> 01:37:17.081
There's no way
we can take Team KAIST down now.

01:37:17.165 --> 01:37:18.958
We should smash Team SNU in Medicine.

01:37:19.042 --> 01:37:20.460
We've got to be bold.

01:37:20.543 --> 01:37:22.045
Hey, they're out to get us.

01:37:22.128 --> 01:37:23.588
Everyone is targeting us.

01:37:23.671 --> 01:37:26.257
This is a major make-or-break move.

01:37:26.341 --> 01:37:28.051
What do we do now? We're in big trouble.

01:37:28.134 --> 01:37:29.093
Yeah, really.

01:37:29.177 --> 01:37:30.887
You could say Team SNU wasted their lives.

01:37:30.970 --> 01:37:32.597
We're seeing the infighting of Team SNUs.

01:37:32.680 --> 01:37:33.848
Let's not get involved.

01:37:33.931 --> 01:37:36.392
- It's better for us.
- Team SNU is practically repaying us.

01:37:36.976 --> 01:37:38.895
We must take a gamble to win.

01:37:39.479 --> 01:37:42.065
Seriously though,
that's absolutely insane.

01:38:24.190 --> 01:38:26.192
Subtitle translation by Jeongwoo Kim